---
// English Terms & Conditions
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms and Conditions - Alpha Sign AG" description="General Terms and Conditions of Alpha Sign AG for signage and advertising technology" lang="en">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">General Terms and Conditions (GTC)</h1>

    <p class="text-gray-600 mb-8">Last updated: January 2025</p>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">1. Scope of Application</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        These General Terms and Conditions (hereinafter "GTC") apply to all contracts,
        deliveries, and services of Alpha Sign AG (hereinafter "Alpha Sign" or "we")
        with its customers (hereinafter "Customer" or "Client").
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Deviating, conflicting, or supplementary general terms and conditions of the
        Customer shall only become part of the contract if and to the extent that we
        have expressly agreed to their validity in writing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">2. Offers and Conclusion of Contract</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">2.1 Offers</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Our offers are non-binding and without obligation. They merely constitute an
        invitation to the Customer to submit a binding offer.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">2.2 Validity of Quotations</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Our written quotations are valid for 30 days from the quotation date, unless
        otherwise stated. After this period, we reserve the right to adjust prices.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">2.3 Conclusion of Contract</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        A contract is only concluded upon our written order confirmation or by
        execution of the order.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">2.4 Changes</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Subsequent changes and additions to the contract require written form.
        Customer change requests after order placement may result in additional
        costs and schedule delays.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">3. Prices and Payment Terms</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">3.1 Prices</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        All prices are in Swiss Francs (CHF), ex works, excluding packaging,
        transport, installation, and value-added tax (VAT), unless otherwise agreed.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">3.2 Payment Terms</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Unless otherwise agreed, the following payment terms apply:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-2">
        <li>For orders over CHF 5,000: 50% deposit upon order placement, balance upon delivery</li>
        <li>For orders under CHF 5,000: Payment within 30 days net from invoice date</li>
        <li>For new customers: Advance payment or payment upon delivery</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">3.3 Default</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        In case of payment default, we are entitled to charge default interest of 5% p.a.
        Further claims for damages are reserved.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">3.4 Retention of Title</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The delivered goods remain our property until full payment of all claims.
        The Customer is obligated to treat the goods with care and, upon request,
        to have the retention of title registered in the retention of title register.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">4. Delivery and Performance</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">4.1 Delivery Times</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Delivery dates and periods are only binding if expressly confirmed by us in
        writing. The delivery period begins on the date of the order confirmation,
        but not before receipt of all documents, approvals, and the agreed deposit
        required for execution.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">4.2 Delivery Delay</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        In case of delivery delay, the Customer must set us a reasonable grace period
        of at least 14 days in writing. Claims for damages due to delivery delay are
        excluded unless there is intent or gross negligence on our part.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">4.3 Force Majeure</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        In case of force majeure (e.g., natural disasters, strikes, pandemics, official
        measures), delivery periods are extended accordingly. We are entitled to withdraw
        from the contract if such circumstances persist.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">4.4 Partial Deliveries</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Partial deliveries are permitted and may be invoiced separately.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">5. Installation</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">5.1 Installation Conditions</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The Customer must ensure that:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-2">
        <li>The installation site is accessible and free of obstacles</li>
        <li>The substrate is suitable for installation</li>
        <li>All necessary permits (e.g., building permits) are available</li>
        <li>Power and water connections are available if required</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">5.2 Additional Costs</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Waiting times and additional effort due to unfulfilled installation conditions
        will be invoiced to the Customer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">6. Warranty and Defect Liability</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">6.1 Warranty Period</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The warranty period is 2 years from delivery or acceptance, unless otherwise
        agreed. Manufacturer warranties apply to lighting and electronic components.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">6.2 Defect Notification</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Recognizable defects must be reported in writing immediately, but no later
        than 8 days after delivery. Hidden defects must be reported immediately
        after discovery.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">6.3 Remedy</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        In case of justified defect claims, we are entitled, at our option, to repair
        or replace the goods. If the repair fails twice, the Customer may demand a
        price reduction or withdrawal from the contract.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">6.4 Exclusion of Warranty</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Warranty is excluded for:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-2">
        <li>Improper handling or use</li>
        <li>Natural wear and aging</li>
        <li>Weather influences on outdoor signage (color changes)</li>
        <li>Modifications or alterations by the Customer or third parties</li>
        <li>Material supplied by the Customer</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">7. Liability</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">7.1 Scope of Liability</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Our liability for slight negligence is excluded. Liability for indirect
        damages, consequential damages, and lost profits is excluded in all cases.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">7.2 Limitation of Liability</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Liability is limited to the order value in all cases.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">8. Intellectual Property</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">8.1 Copyrights</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        All designs, drawings, layouts, and other documents created by us remain
        our intellectual property. They may not be reproduced, modified, or passed
        on to third parties without our consent.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">8.2 Usage Rights</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Usage rights to designs are only transferred to the Customer upon full payment.
        Designs not executed will be invoiced separately.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">8.3 Material Provided by the Customer</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The Customer guarantees that logos, images, and texts provided by them are
        free from third-party rights. The Customer indemnifies us against all
        third-party claims resulting from infringement of intellectual property rights.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">9. Cancellation and Withdrawal</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">9.1 Cancellation by the Customer</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        In case of cancellation by the Customer, the following costs are due:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-2">
        <li>Before production start: 25% of the order value</li>
        <li>After production start: 50% of the order value</li>
        <li>For completed goods: 100% of the order value</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">9.2 Withdrawal by Alpha Sign</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        We are entitled to withdraw from the contract if the Customer fails to
        meet payment obligations or insolvency proceedings are opened against
        their assets.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">10. Data Protection</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The collection and processing of personal data is carried out in accordance
        with our <a href="/en/privacy-policy/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">11. Final Provisions</h2>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">11.1 Written Form</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Changes and additions to these GTC require written form. This also applies
        to the waiver of the written form requirement.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">11.2 Severability Clause</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Should individual provisions of these GTC be or become invalid, this shall
        not affect the validity of the remaining provisions. The invalid provision
        shall be replaced by a valid provision that comes closest to the economic
        purpose of the invalid provision.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">11.3 Applicable Law</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Swiss law applies exclusively, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts
        for the International Sale of Goods (CISG).
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-xl font-medium mb-3 mt-6">11.4 Jurisdiction</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The exclusive place of jurisdiction for all disputes arising from or in
        connection with these GTC is Hunenberg, Switzerland.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Contact</h2>
      <address class="not-italic p-4 bg-gray-50 rounded-lg">
        <strong>Alpha Sign AG</strong><br />
        Industriestrasse 15<br />
        6331 Hunenberg<br />
        Switzerland<br /><br />
        Phone: +41 41 780 05 05<br />
        Email: info@alpha-sign.ch
      </address>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>
